linuxmuster-radius (7.3.0) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Switch to the linuxmuster.net version scheme (7.<line>.<n>, distribution lmn73).
  * debian/changelog is the single version source: the .deb, the Python package
    and GET /v1/version all report it (no more hand-edited version in four files).
  * Add `lmnradius test <instance> [--user <name>]`: domain-login diagnostics
    from the console. Without --user a winbind trust check (the "machine account
    deleted" case); with --user one real ntlm_auth MSCHAPv2 run (password + wifi
    gate, exactly the server's mschap path) plus a per-SSID gate preview.
    NT_STATUS_* codes are translated, --json for scripts, exit code as the
    assertion; the password is prompted hidden and never logged or stored. New
    endpoint POST /v1/instances/{name}/test with strict username validation.
  * `lmnradius logs` prints real log lines instead of a JSON blob with escaped
    newlines; --json keeps the wrapped form for scripts.
  * Security fix for servers upgraded from 0.1.6 or earlier: the postinst now
    clears the group/world write bits under /opt/linuxmuster-radius on every
    configure. Those releases shipped that tree world-writable; an upgrade reset
    the files but left 421 directories at 0777 -- among them the venv's
    site-packages, where any local user could drop a .pth file that then executes
    as lmnradius, who is in the docker group.
  * Quieter auth log: the stunnel LDAP-TLS terminator runs at debug=4 (warnings
    and errors only); takes effect with the next image update.
  * Add `make deb`; CI builds the package in ghcr.io/linuxmuster/lmndev-runner:24.04
    and install-smokes it on ubuntu-24.04; a tag v<version> releases it after a
    tag == changelog gate (replaces build-deb.yml).
  * Unify the maintainer address to Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>.
  * docs: linuxmuster-import-devices deletes any machine account without a
    devices.csv row, which kills every login until `lmnradius restart` re-joins;
    register the RADIUS VM in devices.csv. install.md no longer hard-codes a
    release version and calls the real-world deployment a pilot.

 -- Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200

linuxmuster-radius (0.1.6) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Windows SSO release: qualified identities (DOMAIN\user, user@realm) are
    canonicalised server-side; bare usernames keep working. The stock ntdomain +
    suffix policies run in the inner tunnel and the entrypoint defines workgroup
    + DNS domain as local realms (strip, stay local, never proxy). Verified on a
    real DC (matrix 9/9); single-label domains do not create a duplicate realm.
  * Pin DEFAULT_IMAGE to the verified identity image.

 -- Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>  Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:05:24 +0200

linuxmuster-radius (0.1.5) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Pin DEFAULT_IMAGE to the auth-logging image, pulled by digest and verified
    against a real DC (fresh state volume, healthy in 18s, PEAP matrix 7/7 with
    --wifi-group all-wifi, VLAN 20/10 decoded).
  * Log auth decisions (log { auth = yes }): `lmnradius logs` shows Login OK /
    Login incorrect with user and reason; passwords are still never logged.
  * The API surfaces the apply-path precondition errors (missing EAP cert with
    the `lmnradius cert issue` hint, missing or unreadable secret file) as 409
    with a plain-text detail instead of a bare Internal Server Error.

